00:58:22,500 --> 00:58:23,660
你是怎么看待设计的
How do you think about design?

1004
00:58:25,020 --> 00:58:29,260
我觉得能和 Jony Ive 一起做设计非常幸运
I feel super lucky to get to work with Johnny Ive on designing.

1005
00:58:30,280 --> 00:58:30,520
设计各种东西
Things.

1006
00:58:31,200 --> 00:58:34,964
我从他身上学到很多，学到他是怎么真正研究一个问题的
And I have Learned so much from him about how he really studies a problem

1007
00:58:34,964 --> 00:58:37,324
在他去找解决方案之前
before trying to get to the solution and not,

1008
00:58:37,324 --> 00:58:41,534
他甚至不让自己太早去想解决方案，直到他真正把问题
not even letting him think too much about the solution until he really designs,

1009
00:58:41,534 --> 00:58:43,320
真正理解透彻
really understands the problem.

1010
00:58:44,400 --> 00:58:48,280
我觉得这是我以前没意识到的关键
And I think this is a key that I didn't appreciate before.

1011
00:58:48,480 --> 00:58:53,720
真正好的设计，更多在于理解问题，而不是灵光一闪
Like, really great design is way more about understanding the problem than the flash of insight.

1012
00:58:53,760 --> 00:58:58,900
如果你急着扑向答案，或过早把自己锁死在某个方案上
And if you try to rush towards the thing or lock yourself too much into the thing,

1013
00:58:58,900 --> 00:59:01,080
你就做不出同样好的成果
um, you will not do as good of a job.

1014
00:59:01,400 --> 00:59:08,920
我认为 iPhone 是人类迄今共同造出的最伟大的技术产品
I think the iPhone is the greatest piece of technology humanity has collectively yet made.

1015
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:10,440
它是个了不起的东西
It is incredible thing.

1016
00:59:11,090 --> 00:59:13,170
但我已经不再喜欢自己和它的关系了
But I don't like love my relationship with it anymore.

1017
00:59:13,970 --> 00:59:16,985
我关掉了通知，所以现在我其实喜欢它多了，对
I turned off my notifications. So I actually like it much better now. Yeah,

1018
00:59:16,985 --> 00:59:18,250
我一直开着勿扰模式
I keep myself on do not disturb.

1019
00:59:18,890 --> 00:59:20,421
那都还不够，我就
That wasn't even enough. I just like,

1020
00:59:20,421 --> 00:59:23,730
我关掉了几乎所有通知，只留极少数几样
I turned off notifications for everything except a very small number of things.

1021
00:59:24,730 --> 00:59:26,762
我从来不开通知，因为我，你懂的
And I never have them on because I just, you know,

1022
00:59:26,762 --> 00:59:28,490
我想看的时候可以自己去看
I can like look at it if I want to look at it.

1023
00:59:28,570 --> 00:59:29,330
连消息应用也是
Even messages apps.

1024
00:59:29,970 --> 00:59:30,730
连消息应用也是
Even messages apps.

1025
00:59:31,280 --> 00:59:33,298
那简直是一次巨大的生活升级
That was like a big life upgrade.

1026
00:59:33,298 --> 00:59:36,960
我把 TikTok 删了，因为它实在太强了
And I deleted TikTok because it was just like too powerful.

1027
00:59:38,040 --> 00:59:40,160
你之前沉迷 TikTok，我……
Uh, you were addicted to TikTok, you know, I.

1028
00:59:40,160 --> 00:59:43,080
我们做 Sora app 的时候发生了件疯狂的事
Uh, so here's a crazy thing that happened when we were building the Sora app.

1029
00:59:43,520 --> 00:59:46,520
我逼自己沉迷 TikTok，因为我就想学一学
I made myself get addicted to TikTok because I wanted to just, like learn.

1030
00:59:46,680 --> 00:59:49,120
我之前其实从没真正用过它
Like I was like, you know, I, I never really used it before.

1031
00:59:49,120 --> 00:59:51,583
顶多是有人发我一个 TikTok 视频之类的
I mean, I had like people would send me a TikTok or whatever,

1032
00:59:51,583 --> 00:59:52,840
但我从没被它吸进去
but I never got sucked into it.

1033
00:59:53,000 --> 00:59:56,858
我当时想，我真的不想做出那种
And I was like, I really don't want to build something that is gonna have

1034
00:59:56,858 --> 00:59:59,800
会吞掉人们时间的东西，可是……
that kind of thing absorb people's time, but not. And.

1035
01:00:00,080 --> 01:00:03,092
但我爱上它了，我爱 TikTok，我真觉得它很棒
I loved it. I loved TikTok. I really thought it was great. Um,

1036
01:00:03,092 --> 01:00:05,200
然后我以为自己能控制它
and then I thought I could like control it.

1037
01:00:05,240 --> 01:00:07,434
我想，哦，这其实还挺好玩的
I was like, oh, you know, it's actually kind of fun,

1038
01:00:07,434 --> 01:00:09,941
但我只在睡前放松时用个十分钟
but I only use it for like 10 minutes to wind down before bed

1039
01:00:09,941 --> 01:00:11,560
而且我完全能掌控它
and I'm like totally in control of it.

1040
01:00:12,400 --> 01:00:14,061
然后有天晚上就变成了一小时
And then it was like an hour one night

1041
01:00:14,061 --> 01:00:17,328
再后来某个周六下午，我在沙发上刷了差不多三小时
and then some Saturday afternoon I was on the couch for like three hours

1042
01:00:17,328 --> 01:00:21,480
我就想，这真的不是我心中 iPhone 该有的样子
and I was like, this is, like, really not what I thought the iPhone was supposed to be about.

1043
01:00:21,740 --> 01:00:27,100
当下我确实很享受，像嗑药一样，但我能看出它对我有害
No, I'm really enjoying in the moment like a drug. But I can tell it's bad for me.

1044
01:00:27,820 --> 01:00:30,835
然后我短暂地又把它控制住了，降到大概五分钟
And then I like briefly got it back under control and I was down to, like, 5,

1045
01:00:30,835 --> 01:00:33,900
一晚十分钟之类的，就睡前放松一下
10 minutes a night, whatever, you know, like a little wind down before bed.

1046
01:00:33,900 --> 01:00:35,180
然后我就想，够了
Then I was just like, enough.

1047
01:00:35,820 --> 01:00:41,143
我觉得 iPhone 很了不起，但我觉得自己没有足够的自控力
I think the iPhone is amazing and yet I did not feel like I had enough self control

1048
01:00:41,143 --> 01:00:46,385
去留着那个 app，我也不觉得消息应用的通知
to keep that app or I did not feel like the notifications on messaging apps were

1049
01:00:46,385 --> 01:00:48,240
对我来说是净收益
like a net good thing for me.

1050
01:00:48,640 --> 01:00:53,694
我相信我们会做出一整套了不起的、漂亮的、真正有用的
And I'm sure we will make an incredible, beautiful, like really helpful,

1051
01:00:53,694 --> 01:00:55,600
能赋能人的设备
empowering set of devices.

1052
01:00:56,680 --> 01:00:58,439
我也确信有人会滥用它们
And I'm also sure that people will misuse them

1053
01:00:58,439 --> 01:01:00,800
会以我们想象不到的方式让人们的生活变糟
and it'll make people's lives worse in ways we can't imagine.

1054
01:01:00,840 --> 01:01:03,993
我们会适应，但强大的技术就是这样
And we'll adapt. But this is a thing about powerful technology.

1055
01:01:03,993 --> 01:01:05,540
你们在发明一种新设备
You're inventing a new device.

1056
01:01:06,420 --> 01:01:10,220
如果你是 Johnny，探索这个问题空间的过程是怎样的
What is that process of exploration through the problem space like if you're Johnny?

1057
01:01:10,900 --> 01:01:12,100
我不替他回答
I don't answer on his behalf.

1058
01:01:12,180 --> 01:01:17,106
不过他之前多少聊过一些，这是他的流程
Um, but okay, he's like talked about this before somewhat, but it's like his process,

1059
01:01:17,106 --> 01:01:19,049
比如他在做一辆车时
you know, when he's doing the car,

1060
01:01:19,049 --> 01:01:21,963
他会去研究整个赛车运动史
he will like go study all the history of motorsport

1061
01:01:21,963 --> 01:01:24,184
然后是各种不同的字体
and then like the different typefaces

1062
01:01:24,184 --> 01:01:28,000
人们用在车厢内文字上的字体，还有材料
that people use for the text in the cabin of a car and the materials.

1063
01:01:28,120 --> 01:01:31,621
以及原因，还有引擎多年来发出的各种声音
And why and like the diff different sounds that engines have made over time

1064
01:01:31,621 --> 01:01:32,920
为什么有些声音更打动人
and why some have appealed.

1065
01:01:33,040 --> 01:01:36,982
他真的会把这些探索写成一本本书
I mean, he'll write literal books of all his explorations of all of these like

1066
01:01:36,982 --> 01:01:39,200
全是这些细到难以置信的小部件
unbelievably detailed small components.

1067
01:01:39,960 --> 01:01:42,538
你们是不是基本上拿了这些书
Did you guys basically take those books and like, try to,

1068
01:01:42,538 --> 01:01:45,280
把它们当训练数据，去做一个 Johnny 模型
like use them as training data to make, like, a Johnny model?

1069
01:01:45,440 --> 01:01:48,760
没有，不过那倒是很值得一试
Um, no, but that would be a great thing to try there.

1070
01:01:48,880 --> 01:01:51,120
是的，他的流程里确实有一部分我搞不懂
Yeah, there is definitely a part of his process that I don't understand.

1071
01:01:51,160 --> 01:01:53,070
研究这部分我能理解
Like I understand the studying.

1072
01:01:54,230 --> 01:01:58,190
把一个很新的概念打磨成很棒的东西，我也能理解
I understand the refinement of a very new concept into something great.

1073
01:01:58,590 --> 01:02:00,218
但中间有一步
But there is like a middle step,

1074
01:02:00,218 --> 01:02:04,539
从真正吃透问题到那个极其新颖的想法之间的灵感
the inspiration that comes from understanding the problem really well to the like

1075
01:02:04,539 --> 01:02:07,670
在我看来像是一瞬间就冒出来的
very novel idea kind of that seems to me to happen all at once.

1076
01:02:07,670 --> 01:02:11,083
我不明白，当你在构思设计一样东西时
And I don't understand that when you're thinking about designing something, how,

1077
01:02:11,083 --> 01:02:12,270
你脑子里在想什么
what goes through your mind?

1078
01:02:13,580 --> 01:02:14,860
反正我不是设计师
I'm not a designer anyway.

1079
01:02:14,940 --> 01:02:16,449
我不会，我不，我，呃
I would, I would not, I, I, uh,

1080
01:02:16,449 --> 01:02:20,031
我尽量清楚地认识到自己不擅长什么
I try to be like pretty good about realizing what I'm not good at and I,

1081
01:02:20,031 --> 01:02:22,420
这方面我不会有太强的看法
I wouldn't try to have a strong opinion there.

1082
01:02:23,220 --> 01:02:26,940
在做公司这一面，你最不擅长什么
What are you the worst at on the business building side?

1083
01:02:27,860 --> 01:02:28,660
也许是产品
Maybe product.

1084
01:02:29,380 --> 01:02:30,100
真的吗？也许吧
Really? Maybe.

1085
01:02:31,540 --> 01:02:34,500
好，如果你不擅长产品，怎么找到优秀的产品人
Okay. How do you find great product people if you're bad at product?

1086
01:02:35,870 --> 01:02:38,590
这一点我一直和别人看法不同
This is a thing that I've never quite agreed with people on.

1087
01:02:38,630 --> 01:02:40,926
商界有种说法
There's like, there's like a, there's like a business meme

1088
01:02:40,926 --> 01:02:43,550
说你只能招你深刻理解的领域里的人
that you can only hire people in things that you deeply understand.

1089
01:02:43,630 --> 01:02:46,870
我觉得只要他们够优秀，这显然不成立
I think it, you know, if they're great. I think this is just clearly not true.

1090
01:02:47,870 --> 01:02:49,836
我也不懂设计，但我知道 Johnny 设计得很好
I don't understand design either. I know Johnny's great design.

1091
01:02:49,836 --> 01:02:51,110
有很多东西我能指出来
Like there's lots of things I can point to.

1092
01:02:51,110 --> 01:02:52,537
你跟他聊上 30 分钟
And you talk to him for 30 minutes,

1093
01:02:52,537 --> 01:02:55,697
很明显能看出哪些事你要主动去变强
it's very obvious which things do you try to actively get better at and then

1094
01:02:55,697 --> 01:02:58,092
哪些事你只需要外包出去，然后接受一点
which things do you just try to outsource and understand

1095
01:02:58,092 --> 01:03:00,080
那就是你永远成不了顶尖
that you're just never gonna be one of the best.

1096
01:03:00,480 --> 01:03:03,771
我坚信你该在自己的强项上继续变强
I am a big believer in you should try to get better at your strengths and the whole,

1097
01:03:03,771 --> 01:03:06,030
而那种执念，非要去补
like, obsession with I'm gonna get better at the things

1098
01:03:06,030 --> 01:03:08,240
那些你根本不擅长、也永远不会擅长的东西
that I'm just not good at all and never gonna be good at.

1099
01:03:08,400 --> 01:03:11,260
那是巨大的陷阱，把强项做到极致就好
Huge trap, super good at your strengths. Okay,

1100
01:03:11,260 --> 01:03:15,000
如果非要排个序，你最大的强项是什么
what are your biggest strengths if you had to like force rank?

1101
01:03:15,240 --> 01:03:18,760
我讨厌这个问题，不是出于假谦虚
I hate this question. Um, I don't hate this from a false modesty perspective.

1102
01:03:18,760 --> 01:03:22,390
而是要对自己的强项说出点洞见，真的很难
I think it's, like, very hard to say anything insightful about your own strengths.

1103
01:03:23,070 --> 01:03:26,310
你显然很擅长把人凝聚到某个目标上
You're clearly good at really rallying people around some objective.

1104
01:03:27,030 --> 01:03:27,390
是的
Sure.

1105
01:03:27,550 --> 01:03:31,179
但我不觉得我能教会一个不擅长这个的人
Uh, but I don't like, I don't think I could teach someone who isn't good at

1106
01:03:31,179 --> 01:03:32,510
怎么把这件事做好
that how to be good at that.

1107
01:03:33,270 --> 01:03:37,233
那些对某人来说天生就会的事，很难
I think the things that come supernaturally to someone are very hard to,

1108
01:03:37,233 --> 01:03:39,347
我说不好，至少就我自己而言
I don't know, or at least in my own case,

1109
01:03:39,347 --> 01:03:43,310
我并不真正理解自己为什么擅长这个，也不知道该拿它怎么办
I don't like deeply understand why I'm good at that or what to do about it.

1110
01:03:43,800 --> 01:03:46,764
不过我们前面聊过这一类东西
Although I think we talked about earlier like this category of things

1111
01:03:46,764 --> 01:03:48,400
你能学会，但没法被教会
that you can learn but you can't teach.

1112
01:03:49,840 --> 01:03:53,039
我觉得理解这点很重要
I think this is quite important to understand and like

1113
01:03:53,039 --> 01:03:57,872
如果你想在这类事上变强，让别人给你讲解
if you want to get good at something like that, asking someone to explain it to you,

1114
01:03:57,872 --> 01:03:59,720
依我的经验，从来没用
in my experience, never works.

1115
01:04:00,560 --> 01:04:02,711
真正去研究他们，跟他们一起开会
Really studying them and like sitting with them in meetings

1116
01:04:02,711 --> 01:04:04,560
然后自己去观察、去学
and just trying to observe it and learn it yourself.

1117
01:04:05,130 --> 01:04:05,970
这才管用
That does work.

1118
01:04:06,650 --> 01:04:10,742
每当有件事我确实想变强
Um, but, and like when there has been something that I do want to get better at,

1119
01:04:10,742 --> 01:04:15,090
我都会去靠近那个做得很好的人，深入研究他
I have tried to just be around someone who's great at it and really deeply study it.

1120
01:04:15,450 --> 01:04:17,210
但我不觉得他们能把这事讲清楚给我听
But I don't think they would have been able to explain it to me.

1121
01:04:17,250 --> 01:04:19,530
我不觉得靠跟我聊他们就能教会我
I don't think they could have like taught it to me by talking to me about it.

1122
01:04:19,850 --> 01:04:21,010
我觉得完全对
I think that's totally right.

1123
01:04:21,010 --> 01:04:24,461
你看世界顶尖玩家怎么学游戏
If you look at like the way that the best people in the world learn video games,

1124
01:04:24,461 --> 01:04:27,050
比如你玩 CS:GO，你先自己打几局
if you're playing, like, CS go, you, like, play some CS go.

1125
01:04:27,090 --> 01:04:30,545
掌握基本的游戏机制，然后去看职业选手
So you have like the basic game dynamics and then you just go watch a pro

1126
01:04:30,545 --> 01:04:32,570
看他们在地图上怎么走位
and like see how they interact on the map.

1127
01:04:32,650 --> 01:04:34,450
在不同阶段百分之百地去研究
hundred % at different points in the game and stuff.

1128
01:04:34,730 --> 01:04:38,659
说到组织、节奏，还有野心
When you think about like organization, pace, you know, there's like ambition,

1129
01:04:38,659 --> 01:04:42,530
这些东西，你理想中希望你的组织随时间推进
all these other things, but like you ideally over time want your organization.

1130
01:04:43,490 --> 01:04:46,610
你当然不希望它变慢，最好还能越跑越快
You obviously don't want it to slow down, but ideally it even moves faster.

1131
01:04:47,370 --> 01:04:51,570
这怎么做到？我觉得九成取决于你放在领导岗上的人
How do you like bake that in? I think it's like 90% the people you put in leadership roles.

1132
01:04:51,920 --> 01:04:54,120
好，还有些别的办法
Okay, there's like other things you can do.

1133
01:04:54,280 --> 01:04:56,412
大家有各种不同的运作节奏
People have all these different sort of operating rhythms

1134
01:04:56,412 --> 01:04:59,240
各种经营公司的方式、各种管理技巧
and how they try to run the company and this management technique and that one.

1135
01:04:59,240 --> 01:05:01,800
但我觉得，最终主要还是取决于人
And I think it's, I think mostly just comes down to the people.

1136
01:05:02,320 --> 01:05:06,042
对每个坐在那种位置上的人，我一定会想的一点是
Definitely something I think about with everybody in a role like that is like,

1137
01:05:06,042 --> 01:05:07,760
他们是行动快的人，还是慢的人
are they a fast mover or a slow mover?

1138
01:05:08,040 --> 01:05:10,560
如果没跟他们共事过，你怎么判断这点
How do you measure that without actually having worked with them in the past?

1139
01:05:11,160 --> 01:05:14,520
理想情况是你以前跟他们共事过，多数时候是这样
Well, ideally, you have worked them in the past. I think most of the time.

1140
01:05:15,460 --> 01:05:19,660
公司的高管应该内部提拔，而不是外部招聘
Executives at a company should be promoted internally, not hired externally. Okay.

1141
01:05:20,020 --> 01:05:23,129
但当你确实需要从外部招人时
Um, but when you do need to hire someone externally,

1142
01:05:23,129 --> 01:05:27,620
你会花很多时间跟他们聊，花很多时间做背景调查
you spend a lot of time talking to them, spend a lot of time reference checking.

1143
01:05:27,780 --> 01:05:30,340
你会试着以某种轻松的方式先一起合作
You try to like work together in some kind of casual way.

1144
01:05:30,900 --> 01:05:32,820
换个话题，过去 12 个月里
Slightly different note, what was the most painful thing

1145
01:05:32,820 --> 01:05:34,020
最痛苦的事是什么
that happened in the last 12 months?

1146
01:05:35,750 --> 01:05:39,098
老实说，一边养孩子一边拼命工作太折磨人了
